    {
      "date": "2026-07-16",
      "description": "Gas prices jump 10 cents to $3.94 amid Strait of Hormuz instability.",
      "details": "The national average for a gallon of regular gasoline increased by 10 cents to $3.94, driven by instability along the Strait of Hormuz and crude oil prices nearing $80 per barrel. This price hike impacts consumer budgets, as gasoline is a significant discretionary expense. Higher fuel costs can reduce disposable income available for other purchases, including premium food items. The ongoing geopolitical tensions affecting oil supply directly influence consumer sentiment and spending on non-essential goods.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "AAA Fuel Prices"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-21",
      "description": "Back-to-school shopping begins early; clothing surpasses supplies as top category.",
      "details": "The back-to-school shopping season commenced earlier than usual in 2026, with nearly half of shoppers starting by July. Clothing and shoes have emerged as the top spending category, surpassing traditional school supplies. This shift indicates a change in consumer priorities, with a greater emphasis on apparel. While back-to-school spending can be a significant driver, the focus on clothing might divert some discretionary funds from other gift-oriented categories. The overall concern for consumers is managing the total budget rather than individual item costs.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "seasonal",
      "icon": "🗓️",
      "mood_impact": "neutral",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "RetailMeNot / Mashable"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-23",
      "description": "National average gas price jumps 15 cents to $4.09 due to Strait of Hormuz volatility.",
      "details": "The national average for gasoline surged by 15 cents to $4.09 per gallon, with most states now averaging $4 or higher. This increase is attributed to rising crude oil prices, exacerbated by volatility along the Strait of Hormuz and regional instability. Such a significant jump in fuel costs directly impacts household budgets, potentially curtailing discretionary spending on non-essential items like premium specialty foods. Consumers facing higher essential costs may reduce spending on gifts and treats.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "high",
      "source": "AAA Newsroom"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-27",
      "description": "Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index dips to 90.8 in July.",
      "details": "The Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index decreased to 90.8 in July, down from 92.2 in June, indicating a slight softening in consumer sentiment. This decline, influenced by ongoing conflict in the Middle East, suggests consumers are becoming more cautious about the present economic situation and future outlook. A reading below 70 typically signals pessimism, but the downward trend itself can lead to reduced discretionary spending as consumers prioritize essentials and become more hesitant about non-essential purchases like premium food gifts.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "The Conference Board"
    },
